   926	to the identity \eqref{almThm2.1} and recalling \eqref{p6}, we find that
   927	 the sums
   928	$$3x^2+3\f{y(y+1)}2+\f{z(3z+1)}2\, \quad  \text{and}\,\quad  3\f{x(x+1)}2+\f{y(3y+1)}2+z(3z+2),$$
   929	 are almost universal in view of the first and second terms of the right-hand side of \eqref{almThm2.1}.
   930	
   931	 (ii) Kane and Sun \cite{KaneSun} showed that the sums
   932	 $$x^2+6y(y+1)+\frac{z(z+1)}{2}\ \ \t{and}\ \ x^2+6y^2+\frac{z(z+1)}{2}$$
   933	are almost universal.  By \eqref{SunLemma1} and \eqref{p6},
   934	  $$x^2+6y(y+1)+\frac{z(z+1)}{2} \sim 12x(2x+1)+y(3y+1)+\frac{z(3z+1)}{2}$$
   935	  and
   936	  $$x^2+6y^2+\frac{z(z+1)}{2} \sim 6x^2+y(3y+1)+\frac{z(3z+1)}{2}.$$
   937	   So the tuples $(24,12,6,2,3,1)$
   938	  and $(12,0,6,2,3,1)$ are almost universal.
